The following date helper functions are available in BOTH the Python sandbox AND
DuckDB SQL (they are defined as DuckDB macros, so use them inside SQL too).
Prefer these over hand-rolling date arithmetic, which is a common source of
errors. Do not redefine them.
<function>
def years_between(a, b) -> float
    """Whole (signed) years between two date-like values. Use for
    tenure/experience: years_between(earlier, later)."""

def as_date(x) -> date
    """Coerce any date-like value (string / timestamp / date) to a DATE.
    Use inside SQL: as_date("[Employee Master[Date of Joining]]")."""

def today() -> date
    """Today's date. Use inside SQL: today()."""
</function>
